+# ADR 0025: AFK runs: one team, a wall-clock budget, and a lead that never waits
+
+Status: accepted, 2026-10-26. Design and reasoning in
+`docs/design/2026-10-19-afk-mode.md`.
+
+## Context
+
+The user wants to type one task and walk away. A teamwire lead today waits
+for a person in several places. It can end a turn on a question that nothing
+will ever answer. Its skill tells it to ask the user, to report
+`TEAM-STALLED`, and to ask before a push. The Mac can sleep during planning,
+because launch takes the sleep hold only when the first member starts. A
+lead that keeps planning has no limit. Members already work with nobody
+present (bypass permissions, the "no human" contract), so only the lead
+changes.
+
+## Decision
+
+1. **One AFK run is one ordinary team.** A nullable column on `team`,
+   `afk_budget_ends_at` (schema version 5), marks the run and says when its
+   budget ends. State lives in `$TEAMWIRE_HOME/teams/<team>/`, and the run's
+   shared files in its `afk/` folder, so close archives them with no new
+   code. Rejected: a separate `afk/` home beside `teams/`, because every
+   reader of team state (status, watch, close, the dashboard) would need a
+   second place to look.
+2. **`teamwire afk start --team --title --task [--budget 8h]`** runs from the
+   lead's shell. It refuses outside a lead session (`no_lead_session`), when
+   the session already leads an open AFK team (`afk_already_running`), on
+   launch's name and title rules, when a doctor check a launch needs fails
+   (`doctor_failed`, naming the check), and when the platform needs a sleep
+   hold and the lead's process is not found (`no_lead_process`). Nothing is
+   created on a refusal. It then creates the team with no members, copies
+   the task to `afk/task.md` byte for byte, records `lead_cwd` on
+   `team.created`, and takes the sleep hold at once. Members join with
+   `teamwire launch --add`, which accepts a team with no members.
+3. **The lead's Stop hook holds an AFK lead once per stop chain** when
+   nothing will wake it. Something will wake it when a team it leads is
+   open, has a started member with no completion for its generation, and has
+   a live watch lease. The hold skips `stop_hook_active` and subagent turns,
+   so a lead whose own background command will wake it can stop on the
+   second try. Rejected: a counter of holds, which would hold forever or
+   need state the hook may not write.
+4. **A wall-clock budget, default 8 hours.** Past it, launch refuses a new
+   `implementer` with `afk_budget_spent` and accepts every other kind, so the
+   run can still review, verify and report. Rejected: a token budget, which
+   the user did not choose.
+5. **Launch warns about a Claude member of an AFK team below the AFK model
+   table**: opus at `high` for implementers and investigators, at `xhigh`
+   for reviewers and the closer. It warns and does not refuse, because the
+   lead may have a reason.
+6. **The run ends with `teamwire close`.** Close refuses an AFK team whose
+   `afk/REPORT.md` is missing or lacks one of the eight headings of the AFK
+   skill, with `refused: afk_report_incomplete`. Rejected: an `afk finish`
+   command, which would duplicate close's safe order and hold release.
+7. **The run's status is the team's status.** `teamwire status` shows one
+   `afk:` line and `--json` an `afk` object (`budget_ends_at`,
+   `seconds_left`, `spent`, `decisions`). `teamwire teams` marks the team
+   `afk`, and `--json` gives every team `afk_budget_ends_at`. Rejected: an
+   `afk status` command.
+8. **The AFK skill is a second skill in the teamwire plugin**,
+   `/teamwire:afk`, rendered by install from `examples/skills/afk/SKILL.md`
+   and checked by doctor with the rest of the plugin's files. It reads the
+   main skill first and lists only what changes. Members do the research,
+   planning, review, verification and the report, to protect the lead's
+   context. Claude Code leads only: a Codex lead keeps today's behaviour.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A lead that stops twice with nothing running is stuck. `teamwire status`
+  shows the AFK team open with no working member.
+- An older binary opens an AFK team's database read only (ADR 0015).
+- A Claude usage limit pauses the lead and members alike. The report's cost
+  section shows it afterwards.
